Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: jdi-lt070me05000: restore brightness at init, sleep in before the stream stops

The DCS soft reset in the init sequence resets the brightness register,
and the only write that restores it is the HS one sent from
backlight_enable() while the video stream starts. On the Nexus 7 (2013)
with the MSM DSI v2 host that write is lost and the panel stays at full
brightness until userspace writes the value again. Program the
brightness in the init sequence.

SET_DISPLAY_OFF and ENTER_SLEEP_MODE were sent from unprepare, after the
host stopped the video stream, where the MSM DSI host times out waiting
for video done (-110). Send them from disable instead.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jdi-lt070me05000.c	2026-11-15 19:37:56.117632473 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jdi-lt070me05000.c	2026-11-15 19:37:56.210539827 +0100
@@ -67,6 +67,17 @@
 	 */
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, MIPI_DCS_WRITE_CONTROL_DISPLAY, 0x24);
 
+	/*
+	 * The soft reset above puts the brightness register back to its
+	 * default. Program the requested level here, in LP mode with the rest
+	 * of the init sequence, instead of relying on the HS write that
+	 * backlight_enable() sends while the video stream is starting. The
+	 * backlight is still marked off here, so use the stored level.
+	 */
+	if (jdi->backlight)
+		mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_multi(&dsi_ctx,
+				jdi->backlight->props.brightness);
+
 	/* CABC off */
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, MIPI_DCS_WRITE_POWER_SAVE, 0x00);
 
@@ -118,6 +128,13 @@
 
 	backlight_disable(jdi->backlight);
 
+	/*
+	 * Send display off and sleep in while the host still runs the video
+	 * stream. Once the stream is stopped the DSI command engine waits for
+	 * a video-done interrupt that never comes and both commands time out.
+	 */
+	jdi_panel_off(jdi);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -127,8 +144,6 @@
 	struct device *dev = &jdi->dsi->dev;
 	int ret;
 
-	jdi_panel_off(jdi);
-
 	ret = regulator_bulk_disable(ARRAY_SIZE(jdi->supplies), jdi->supplies);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		dev_err(dev, "regulator disable failed, %d\n", ret);
